NEARS-2428 QA regression note (pre-existing, unrelated to this ticket's diff)
— sibling Admin/app/CentralLogics/helpers.php::sendNotificationToHttp() logs
raw request payload / response body, violating the logging-contract
allow-list rule. Untouched by this ticket (diff is confined to
Admin/app/Traits/NotificationTrait.php); filed as regression_bugs, does not
affect this ticket's PASS/FAIL.

Admin/app/CentralLogics/helpers.php (excerpt, line numbers from worktree HEAD):
1455-1458:
    if (!data_get($key, 'project_id')) {
        \Log::warning('FCM config missing - no project_id', ['data' => $data]);
        return false;
    }
1461-1464:
    $token = self::getAccessToken($key);
    if (!$token) {
        \Log::error('FCM access token is null/empty', ['data' => $data]);
        return false;
    }
1484-1489 (failure branch):
    } else {
        \Log::error('FCM API Error', [
            'status' => $response->status(),
            'body' => $response->body(),
            'order_id' => $data['message']['data']['order_id'] ?? 'unknown',
        ]);

$data here is the full outbound FCM message payload, which for a
device-targeted send (sendPushNotificationToDevice) includes
$data['message']['token'] — the raw FCM device token — plus the full
notification title/body. $response->body() on the failure branch is the raw
FCM error response body. Both are logged verbatim to laravel.log, contrary
to docs/platform/logging-contract.md's "never log response bodies, request
payloads, tokens" rule.

Additionally, the success line at this same file (Log::info('FCM Send
Success', ...)) is subject to the identical LOG_LEVEL=warning filtering
documented in bug-success-log-level-filtered.log — it also silently never
reaches laravel.log under the project's standard config.

Not filed as a task_bug against NEARS-2428: this code path was not touched
by the diff under QA (git diff dd9a2a2c -- Admin/app/Traits/NotificationTrait.php
only). Recommend a follow-up ticket to align helpers.php's
sendNotificationToHttp() with the same PII-safe pattern this ticket applied
to NotificationTrait.php's copy.
